
Before installing:

Create S3 bucket.
Create IAM Role with policies: AmazonS3FullAccess (or least-privilege), AmazonEC2FullAccess (for snapshots), and trust relationship for EKS Pod Identity.
Attach the role to Velero's ServiceAccount via Pod Identity Association.


helm repo add vmware-tanzu https://vmware-tanzu.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

helm install velero vmware-tanzu/velero \
  --namespace velero \
  --create-namespace \
  --values velero-values.yaml


## Do this after installing Velero with this values.yaml to set up Pod Identity:

aws eks create-pod-identity-association \
  --cluster-name <your-cluster-name> \
  --namespace velero \
  --service-account velero \
  --role-arn arn:aws:iam::YOUR_ACCOUNT:role/velero-role


After install:

Create a VolumeSnapshotClass for EBS CSI with label velero.io/csi-volumesnapshot-class: "true".
Test a backup: velero backup create test-backup --include-namespaces default --wait